Although all three queries return the same numbers for the current snapshot of the data, `1result.sql` is the most robust and therefore the correct choice:

• It joins the two tables case‑insensitively with `LOWER( … )`, avoiding missed matches caused by simple spelling‑case differences.  
• It counts ADA‑qualified stations directly in the join instead of through an extra CTE, keeping the logic concise while still de‑duplicating with `COUNT(DISTINCT … )`.  
• It uses `SAFE_DIVIDE` (via `SAFE_DIVIDE` or its arithmetic equivalent) so the percentage calculation cannot throw a division‑by‑zero error.  

```plaintext
1result.sql
```